From: Moacyr Prado <mwprado@github>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] apex: fix reset error handling and probe retry delay

apex_pci_probe() ignored the return value from apex_reset(), allowing probe
to continue after a failed hardware reset.

The readiness loop also used schedule_timeout() while the current task
remained TASK_RUNNING. In that state schedule_timeout() does not provide the
intended millisecond sleep, so the nominal 12 second retry window can collapse
into a tight scheduler loop.

Use msleep(), matching the millisecond APEX_RESET_DELAY constant and the
existing wait helper used elsewhere in this driver, and stop probing if the
initial reset fails.

---
 src/apex_driver.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apex_driver.c b/src/apex_driver.c
--- a/src/apex_driver.c
+++ b/src/apex_driver.c
@@ -1007,7 +1007,12 @@ static int apex_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pci_dev,
 	apply_module_params(apex_dev);
 	program_hw_temp_warnings(apex_dev);
 	pci_set_drvdata(pci_dev, apex_dev);
-	apex_reset(gasket_dev);
+	ret = apex_reset(gasket_dev);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(&pci_dev->dev, "error resetting Apex device: %d\n",
+			ret);
+		goto remove_device;
+	}
 
 	while (retries < APEX_RESET_RETRY) {
 		page_table_ready =
@@ -1021,7 +1026,7 @@ static int apex_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pci_dev,
 					   APEX_BAR2_REG_KERNEL_HIB_MSIX_TABLE_INIT);
 		if (page_table_ready && msix_table_ready)
 			break;
-		schedule_timeout(msecs_to_jiffies(APEX_RESET_DELAY));
+		msleep(APEX_RESET_DELAY);
 		retries++;
 	}
 
